[
    {
        "text": "Crypto lending works by taking crypto from one user and providing it to another with interest. In most cases, the loan taker must put up some collateral before borrowing any crypto. On the other side of the loan, you may have a smart contract that mints stablecoins to lend out, or a platform lending out funds from another user. The exact method of managing the process changes from platform to platform. You can find crypto lending services on centralized and decentralized platforms, but the core principles remain the same. Crypto borrowing and lending is usually done without credit checks, and loan transactions are settled instantly. These features could be a boon or a bane. You need to be careful with various risks that could lead to losses.",
        "start": 320,
        "end": 45900,
        "confidence": 0.9894472,
